        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.093,
            0.744,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": " The eight planets, in order of their increasing distance from the Sun, are Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.158,
            0.739,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": " The Earth revolves around the Sun in nearly one year."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.182,
            0.743,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": " Objects that move around planets are commonly called satellites."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.227,
            0.552,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": " The Moon is Earth’s natural satellite."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.25,
            0.743,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": " The Moon revolves around the Earth in nearly 27 days."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.275,
            0.744,
            0.337
          ],
          "content": "The Sun, eight planets, their moons, and many smaller objects including asteroids and comets, together form the Solar System."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.34,
            0.688,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": "Our Solar System is part of the Milky Way Galaxy."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.407,
            0.611,
            0.431
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Let us enhance our learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.613,
            0.372,
            0.728,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.459,
            0.348,
            0.48
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "1. Match the column:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.486,
            0.741,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": "| Column I | Column II |\n| --- | --- |\n| (i) Satellite of Earth | (a) Orion |\n| (ii) Red planet | (b) Venus |\n| (iii) Constellation | (c) Mars |\n| (iv) Planet which is commonly called an evening star | (d) Moon |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_18_table_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.662,
            0.455,
            0.682
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "2. (i) Solve the following riddle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.686,
            0.641,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "My first alphabet is in MAN but not in CAN My second alphabet is in ACE and also in FAN My third alphabet is in RAT and not in CAT My fourth alphabet is in SUN but not in FUN I am a planet that moves around the Sun."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.81,
            0.563,
            0.831
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Make two similar riddles by yourself."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.839,
            0.743,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": "3. Which of the following is not a member of our Solar System? (i) Sirius (ii) Comets (iii) Asteroids (iv) Pluto"
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
